  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The solid "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " granny removes both the chain-1 side gaps and the chain-2 corner space on the sides, replacing every gap with a single treble worked into the top of the previous cluster stitch. Only the four corner ch-2 spaces remain open, as they are needed to keep the corners square. The result is a genuinely solid fabric, heavier and more insulating than a standard granny, and well suited for pot holders, cold-weather blankets, and any project where draping opacity rather than lightness is the goal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 28 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, blocking mat and pins (optional)."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4 rounds in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 10 x 10 cm after blocking. The solid construction uses more yarn per square than a standard granny; allow approximately 25 per cent more yardage when substituting this motif for the standard version in a project."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
