      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Note: ch 3 counts as first tr throughout."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. Ch 2. *(3 tr into ring, ch 2)*; repeat 3 more times. Pull tail to close. Join with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "slip-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "sl st"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to top of ch 3. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to the ch-2 corner space. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into the corner space. *Work 1 tr into the top of each of the 3 side tr of the previous round (no ch-1 gap), then (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into the next ch-2 corner space*; repeat from * to * 3 more times. Work 1 tr into each of the remaining side tr. Join with sl st to top of ch 3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to the ch-2 corner space. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp, then 1 tr into the top of every tr along the side (6 tr per side)*; repeat from * to * 3 more times. End with (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in last corner, then 1 tr in each remaining side tr. Join with sl st. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work as round 3, increasing the side treble count to 9 tr per side. Join with sl st. Fasten off. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "slug": "crochet-motif-granny-solid-treble"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in tails. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Block"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " by pinning each corner to 90 degrees on a blocking mat, with the four corner points pinned first and the side edges eased to straight lines."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join solid granny squares with a flat sl st join through the outer edge stitches or a mattress stitch seam. Both methods keep the edge as solid as the body."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 °C gentle cycle or hand wash. Lay flat to dry. The dense fabric dries slowly; allow extra time."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The puff stitch square adds raised texture to the side positions of a granny square while keeping the corner structure identical to this motif. The lace square motif is the opposite direction: it opens the sides further with chain arches."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
